{
 "schema": "worldloom.contract-lock/v1",
 "about": "The vendor contract each connector is served behind through Anvil, pinned by the sha256 of its exact bytes. `worldloom contracts fetch` downloads each vendor source (or copies an authored one out of the package) and refuses bytes that hash to anything else; `worldloom contracts build CONNECTOR` compiles it under its profile with Anvil; `worldloom contracts coverage` reports what each profile exposes and what the mapping models. vendor_operations counts the whole source; profiled_operations is what the profile exposes and the mapping must cover. anvil_source_hash is Anvil's snapshot identity for the locked bytes. anvil_profile names Anvil's own reviewed profile for the same source (in the Anvil repository), whose source pin agrees with this digest; the Worldloom profile is narrower, the operations the connector models and their neighbours.",
